-- title:
--   Value of Λ at U_q for q exactly dividing M
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$, let $\varepsilon$ be a Dirichlet character modulo $M$ with values in $\mathbb C$, and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form for $\Gamma_1(M)$ which is a primitive form with nebentypus $\varepsilon$, i.e. $a_1(g)=1$, the relations $a_{\ell n}(g)+\varepsilon(\ell)\,\ell^{k-1}\,[\ell\mid n]\,a_{n/\ell}(g)=a_\ell(g)a_n(g)$ hold for all primes $\ell\nmid M$ and all $n$, $a_{\ell n}(g)=a_\ell(g)a_n(g)$ for all primes $\ell\mid M$ and all $n$, $g$ has nebentypus $\varepsilon$, and for no proper divisor $M'\mid M$ does the eigenpacket $(a_n(g),\varepsilon(n))$ occur at level $M'$ (no nonzero form of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_1(M')$ with some nebentypus satisfies the corresponding relations with the coefficients $a_\ell(g)$ outside a finite set of primes). Let $p$ be a prime, assume the predicates [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsAll M`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L58) (existence of the Hecke inputs along every prime for $X_1(M)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and of diamond automorphisms for every $d$ coprime to $M$ together with their base changes to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondCommuteBar M`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L54) (the Hecke and diamond generators on the base-changed function field commute pairwise). Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals, $\Omega$ a field that is a $\mathbb Q_p$-algebra, $R$ a commutative ring, $t\colon R\to\mathbb C$ an injective ring homomorphism, $\psi\colon R\to\Omega$ a ring homomorphism, and $b,e\colon\mathbb N\to R$ with $t(b_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$ and $t(e_\ell)=\varepsilon(\ell)$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$. Let $q$ be a prime with $q\mid M$, $q^2\nmid M$, $q\nmid\operatorname{cond}(\varepsilon)$, and $t(b_q)=a_q(g)$. Give $J_1(M)$, the degree-zero divisor class group of the base-changed $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(M)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, its Hecke-algebra module structure `heckeModuleOneBar M`, and let $A$ be the $\mathbb Q_p$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb Q_p}(\mathbb Q_p\otimes_{\mathbb Z_p}T_pJ_1(M))$ generated by the images of the Hecke and diamond generators. Then for every ring homomorphism $\Lambda\colon A\to\Omega$ which is the identity on $\mathbb Q_p$-scalars and satisfies $\Lambda(T_\ell)\,\psi(e_\ell)=\psi(b_\ell)$ and $\Lambda(\langle\ell\rangle)\,\psi(e_\ell)=1$ for all primes $\ell\nmid M$ outside $S$, and for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ outside $S$ with $\ell\equiv q \pmod{M/q}$, one has $\Lambda(T_q)\,\psi(e_\ell)=\psi(b_q)$, where $T_q$ denotes `rationalHeckeOne p (JOne M) ⟨q, hq⟩`, the generator attached to the prime $q$ dividing $M$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the transfer of a primitive form's eigenvalue packet to the $p$-adic Hecke–diamond algebra acting on the rational Tate module of $J_1(M)$: at a prime $q$ exactly dividing the level with nebentypus unramified at $q$, the packet away from $M$ already pins down the value of any such character on the operator at $q$, normalised by $\psi(e_\ell)$ for any auxiliary prime $\ell\equiv q \bmod M/q$. It is used to read off $a_q(g)$ on the associated $p$-adic Galois representations, in the description of the ordinary line and of Frobenius characteristic polynomials at $q$.
